/ref 17592186539712 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539972 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539972 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539972 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186539491 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539972 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "94f7bcdd-1a29-50a3-b5ca-fac98fc4f9d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539980 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186539871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539980 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539980 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539980 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186539871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186539980 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "aafd742f-ff73-5b71-bc91-fdad1d0edbed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540035 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186539953 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540035 #edb/ref 1069 "q-352750" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540035 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540035 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that\n\n$$\nS={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{(-1)}^{n}}{{e}^{n+2}}\n$$\n\nand that ${s}_{6}$ is the sixth partial sum of $S.$ According to the alternating series error bound, $|S-{s}_{6}|<k$ for some real number $k.$\n\nFind the value of $k.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$k=$\n\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540035 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "26d0f888-4d20-5d31-b520-f4c4f17a1d7e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540035 #edb/ref 1074 "Let ${a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{{e}^{n+2}}$ and ${b}_{n}=\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{e}^{n+2}}.$ Then ${a}_{n}$ is positive and decreasing for $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty .$ So, the series is convergent by the alternating series test.\n\nBecause our series is a convergent alternating series, the alternating series error bound applies. In particular, for the $6$th partial sum, it states that\n\n$$\n|S-{s}_{6}|<|{b}_{7}|=|\\frac{{(-1)}^{7}}{{e}^{7+2}}|=\\frac{1}{{e}^{9}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\frac{1}{{e}^{9}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540077 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186539980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540077 #edb/ref 1069 "q-352755" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540077 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540077 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that\n\n$$\nS={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{(-2)}^{n}}{(n+1)!}\n$$\n\nand that ${s}_{5}$ is the fifth partial sum of $S.$ According to the alternating series error bound, $|S-{s}_{5}|<k$ for some real number $k.$ Find the value of $k.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$k=$\n\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540077 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a26aabae-4ded-5132-8e5c-c91af894cefb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540077 #edb/ref 1074 "Let ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{2}^{n}}{(n+1)!}$ and ${b}_{n}=\\frac{{(-2)}^{n}}{(n+1)!}.$ Then ${a}_{n}$ is positive and decreasing for $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty .$ So, the series is convergent by the alternating series test.\n\nBecause our series is a convergent alternating series, the alternating series error bound applies. In particular, for the $5$th partial sum, it states that\n\n$$\n|S-{s}_{5}|<|{b}_{6}|=|\\frac{{(-2)}^{6}}{(6+1)!}|=\\frac{64}{5040}=\\frac{4}{315}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\frac{4}{315}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540079 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186539941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540079 #edb/ref 1069 "q-83612" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540079 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540079 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that\n\n$$\nS={\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}-1}\n$$\n\nand that ${s}_{i}$ is the $i$th partial sum of $S,$ use the alternating series error bound to determine an inequality that gives the values of $i$ such that $|S-{s}_{i}|<0.1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540079 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aa9e57c4-993f-58af-8f8c-2c21d29224b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540079 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let ${a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}-1}$ and ${b}_{n}=\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}-1}.$ Then ${a}_{n}$ is decreasing for $n\\ge 2$ and ${a}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty .$ So, the series is convergent by the alternating series test. \n\nBecause our series is a convergent alternating series, the alternating series error bound applies. In particular, for the $i$th partial sum, it states that\n\n$$\n|S-{s}_{i}|<|{b}_{i+1}|.\n$$\n\nSo, we require\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{b}_{i+1}|=|\\frac{(-1)^{i+1}}{(i+1)^{2}-1}| & \\le 0.1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{i}^{2}+2i+1-1} & \\le \\frac{1}{10} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{i}^{2}+2i} & \\le \\frac{1}{10} \\\\ {i}^{2}+2i & \\ge 10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540086 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186539972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540086 #edb/ref 1069 "q-104031" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540086 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540086 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that\n\n$$\nS={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{2}^{n}}\n$$\n\nand that ${s}_{i}$ is the $i$th partial sum of $S,$ use the alternating series error bound to determine an inequality that gives the values of $i$ such that $|S-{s}_{i}|<0.01.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540086 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bb487298-b519-5edb-8e52-6ad72f9356fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540086 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let ${a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{{2}^{n}}$ and ${b}_{n}=\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{2}^{n}}.$ Then ${a}_{n}$ is decreasing for $n\\ge 1$ and ${a}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty .$ So, the series is convergent by the alternating series test. \n\nBecause our series is a convergent alternating series, the alternating series error bound applies. In particular, for the $i$th partial sum, it states that\n\n$$\n|S-{s}_{i}|<|{b}_{i+1}|.\n$$\n\nSo, we require\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{b}_{i+1}|=|\\frac{(-1)^{i+1}}{{2}^{i+1}}| & \\le 0.01 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{2}^{i+1}} & \\le \\frac{1}{100} \\\\ 100 & \\le {2}^{i+1} \\\\ 100 & \\le 2\\cdot {2}^{i} \\\\ {2}^{i} & \\ge 50.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540131 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186540139 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540131 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3d748b43-7f4a-55a5-b9f2-b2b1e447b3e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540131 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186540086 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540139 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186540174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540139 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "52608748-4925-5f07-89c8-df6f306d09b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540139 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186540035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540154 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186540131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540154 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "82473a92-9dc4-5f79-bf3f-843f63c36ff6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540154 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186540079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540174 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e0477d66-d0da-57fe-ae64-7a88c2a0d0bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540174 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186540077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540177 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186540154 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540177 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e78a6e2d-2359-5c60-b93c-2d7ced996f4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186540177 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186101467 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
